  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math> sol has negatively charged sol particles and therefore, positive ions are effective in causing the coagulating of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math> sol. <br/>Coagulating efficiencies of electrolytes increase with the increase in the valence of effective ion. Therefore, the best electrolyte for coagulating <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math> sol is <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><msub><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> . <br/><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>",
